Subject: CK: store the exact per-row max logit next to the FMHA forward LSE

Add fmha_fwd_args::max_ptr (fp32, same layout and strides as lse_ptr) for
the max logit used by QK-clip / MuonClip: the max of the softmax inputs over
the unmasked keys, excluding the sink, -inf for fully masked rows.

The instances that store it are chosen at compile time by a kStoreRowMax
parameter of TileFmhaTraits and fmha_fwd_traits_; the dispatch selects them
when max_ptr is set. Receipt 700 gets a _max variant of every qr, qr_async
and qr_async_trload instance that stores the LSE and has no bias or dropout,
sink instances included. All other instances keep their names and generate
the same code as before, so callers that do not ask for the max pay nothing.
With max_ptr set and no matching instance, fmha_fwd returns -1.

The pipelines keep an exact running row max, updated before the conditional
rescale that can leave m up to 8 log2 units below it (from m_local when a
sink seeds m), and store it next to the LSE in the same units. Masked
qr_async row-max instances with 32 < d <= 64 ask for four blocks per CU,
which the extra register would otherwise drop to three.

